ng that documentation is \"clear and comprehensive\" (as Recital 71 demands) is not automatable in any meaningful sense. -points\n- \"Real-time\": Overpromised. -minor points\n\nOverall: I'd approve this as a useful engineering initiative with moderate promise, because the core deliverable (version-controlled, auto-updating technical docs tied to code/dataset changes) genuinely improves prototyping workflow by reducing manual documentation overhead. But I'd flag that the \"automated regulatory audit\" component is where I'd push back on scope.\n\nPromise: 58. It's useful but the proposal as framed includes elements that will consume disproportionate resources relative to their engineering value.\n",
