ing savings are significant - every hour a scientist spends writing compliance docs is an hour not spent on research or building new models. It leverages existing R&D infrastructure effectively. It doesn't compete with scientific ambition; it protects the time that enables scientific ambition by handling regulatory overhead.\n\nI would approve this. Promise score: This is very well-aligned with my domain concerns. The main risk is implementation complexity and whether \"automatic\" actually works reliably enough, but conceptually it's a clear win on resource efficiency. I'd put it around 82-85. Let me settle on 84 - it's strong but there are some implementation risks around the completeness of what gets auto-generated vs. what still needs human curation (e.g., \"capabilities and limitations\" narrative, risk-management documentation).\n\nLet me finalize: approve, promise 84.\n",
