al 71 elements, trigger mechanism might be too narrow, no mention of human review/accountability for content accuracy) but the core idea is sound and directly relevant to my function's mandate. I'd approve it with reservations noted in rationale.\n\nPromise score: From a compliance perspective, this is very promising - maybe 78-82. It addresses a clear regulatory obligation, reduces audit risk, and the automation aspect ensures timeliness. But it has scope gaps and lacks mention of human accountability for generated content. I'll go with 80.\n",
