r-hour freed up from writing compliance docs is an hour spent on actual R&D.\n\nI'd approve this. The promise score should reflect strong alignment with my concerns but also acknowledge some execution risk (scope creep, maintenance burden of the engine itself). I'd put it around 82-85. It's clearly worth pursuing, leverages existing assets well, and has clear ROI in researcher productivity. Not a perfect 100 because \"engine\" projects can drift, and there's ongoing maintenance cost, but from a resource-efficiency standpoint this is one of the better investments available.\n\nLet me settle on 83.\n",
