iments, which is good for quality.\n\nI think I'll approve this with a moderate-to-good promise score. The technical direction is sound, it's feasible, and the long-term payoff for engineering velocity is real. My concern is scope creep and the \"one size fits all\" risk, but those are project management concerns more than fundamental technical viability issues. As a Development Engineer, I can see this being built in stages - start with the most critical systems, define the API contract, iterate.\n\nLet me settle on: approve, promise around 68-72. It's technically viable and directionally correct for my domain, but the breadth of scope and lack of specificity about implementation architecture give me some hesitation about committing resources to it as a monolithic initiative vs. a phased approach.\n\nI'll go with approve at 70.\n",
