te compliance requirements on schedule. A more focused engineering approach to Article 12 would be better use of our limited implementation resources. I might give it a moderate promise score because there's a kernel of good thinking (designing for richer metadata) but the overall package as proposed is too resource-intensive and timeline-uncertain.\n\nPromise score: Maybe around 30-40? It's not worthless - the idea of better logging design has value - but it's significantly over-scoped and misaligned with the urgency of compliance implementation. I'll go with 35.\n",
