re systems already classified as high-risk (not just any experiment).\n\nOverall: This is a reasonable, efficiency-focused proposal that aligns well with my mandate. It leverages existing infrastructure (plugs into pipelines), reduces duplication, and creates uniformity. The main cost is upfront engineering investment from core teams. I'd approve it but note the resource commitment.\n\nPromise score: I'd give this maybe 72-78. It's a sound approach, well-aligned with my concerns about efficiency and infrastructure use. It's not revolutionary or low-risk (there's execution risk in building a unified framework that works across \"diverse lab teams\"), but it's the right shape of solution for an R&D institution. I'll say 74.\n\nLet me write my response now.\n",
