arch potential, but as stated it doesn't clear my bar for frontier research with clear intellectual merit.\n\nLet me settle on: reject, promise 48. The underlying question is legitimate and could be elevated to genuine research, but the proposal as written is an applied engineering task dressed up in research language (\"scientific opportunity\"). Without a clearer articulation of what novel scientific insight or methodological advance it would produce, it doesn't meet my bar for committing scarce implementation resources from a research merit standpoint.\n",
