ddressed in scoping.\n\nGiven that Article 12 mandates this capability for ALL high-risk AI systems, and the lab presumably has multiple such projects, the redundancy-elimination argument is very strong. This isn't speculative R&D — it's a compliance requirement that every team will need to implement anyway. Building it once centrally is clearly more efficient than building it N times independently.\n\nI would approve this. Promise score: I'd give it around 82-85. It's very well-aligned with my domain concerns, directly addresses a regulatory mandate, and the efficiency argument is compelling. The slight deductions are for the centralized-vault complexity risk and the assumption that all deployments can fit into one base image without friction.\n\nLet me settle on 84.\n",
